You can use `ArgumentException` in .NET to signify that an argument has been passed to a function that is invalid in some way. In this case, trying to add a duplicate software to the collection would be considered as providing an "invalid" argument.

Here's an example of using `ArgumentException`:

```csharp
public void AddSoftware(Software software)
{
