Corrections made:

1. I improved the regex to more accurately match email addresses as follows:

    - [\w.+-]+: Matches one or more word characters (letters, numbers, underscores), periods, plus signs, or hyphens.

    - @: Matches the @ symbol.

    - ([\w-]+\.[\w.-]+): Matches the domain part of the email. Inside the parentheses (which also captures the match for use with $1), it matches one or more word characters, hyphens, periods, or underscores. The \. matches a period, then the rest is a repeat of the earlier character class. It will caputre all that come after @ until a space is hit.

