config.kit.adapter should be an object with an "adapt" method, rather than the name of an adapter.

The error `config.kit.adapter should be an object with an "adapt" method, rather than the name of an adapter.` means that the adapter should not be just the name of an adapter package, but an instance of any of those adapters.

So the configuration should look like follow:

```javascript
import adapter from '@sveltejs/adapter-auto';
import firebaseAdapter from 'svelte-adapter-firebase';

/** @type {import('@sveltejs/kit').Config} */
const config = {
    kit: {
        // apply adapter-auto or firebaseAdapter,
        // not both at the same time
        adapter: adapter(), // for adapter-auto
        // adapter: firebaseAdapter(), // for firebaseAdapter
    },
};

export default config;
```

Here, `adapter()` and `firebaseAdapter()` are function calls that create the instances of the adapters. 

Use either `adapter()` or `firebaseAdapter()`, not both at the same time. Depending on the deployment platform, one or the other will be needed.

There is currently no support for using two adapters at the same time in SvelteKit.

