This is clean and communicates the error well, without needing any custom exceptions.

However, if you have many similar validation rules or if this validation is something complex, you might want to consider creating your own custom exception to make your exceptions more expressive and easily identifiable. This would make your code easier to read and maintain in the long run. Here's an example:

```csharp
public class DuplicateSoftwareException : Exception
{
