        temp = nums[i];
        nums[j] = temp;
      }
```
Should look like this:
```java
if(nums[i]>nums[j]) {
        temp = nums[i];
        nums[i] = nums[j];
        nums[j] = temp;
      }
```
We should update both `nums[i]` and `nums[j]` during swap, not just `nums[j]` as it was in the initial function.

So the correct function is:
```java
public static int[] sortArray(int[] nums) {
  int temp;
  for(int i=0; i<nums.length; i++) {
    for(int j=i+1; j<nums.length; j++) {
      if(nums[i]>nums[j]) {
        temp = nums[i];
        nums[i] = nums[j];
        nums[j] = temp;
      }
    }
  }
  return nums;
}
